\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces On the left, the shape the wave settles into, with the point where the flow is at rest marked. Nothing about it looks wrong. On the right, the curvature of that same shape near that same point, which does not pass through zero but leaps across it. The small ripples either side are an artefact of measuring curvature, not part of the shape.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
